IMPORT prelude

-- Nanyang Technological University (Corporatisation) Act 2005 (Singapore) -- what the Minister must consent to and what happens
-- without consent (s 7), how the State's money may be spent (s 8), the duty to give the Minister information and its offence (s 9),
-- the Students' Union and the Societies Act (ss 10, 18), what carried over on 1 April 2006 for litigants, contracting parties,
-- staff and students (ss 12(6), (7), 13-17), and the Register of Graduates (s 19 and the Schedule).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NTUCA2005.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment annotated in the
-- body is [40/2018] at s 7(2) (the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, s 497, in force 30 July 2020 per the
-- Legislative History). Retrieval metadata: "Current version as at 03 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0187 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is short (19 sections and a Schedule), so this row covers nearly all of it that reaches a person.
-- Not encoded: s 3 (function), s 4 (accountability and quality assurance), s 5 (ministerial policy directions), s 6 (Minister
-- appoints and removes trustees), s 11(2), s 12(1)-(5) (the vesting of property, its trusts, the Minister for Finance's conclusive
-- certificate and the President's tenure terms), and s 10(2) beyond the fact of an exemption.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD so that they compare in order (20060401 is 1 April 2006).

§ `Nanyang Technological University (Corporatisation) Act 2005`

`the appointed day` MEANS 20060401

§§ `7 -- what needs the Minister's prior written consent`

-- s 7(1): "The prior written consent of the Minister is required for -- (a) the admission of any person as a member of the university
-- company and the removal of any such member; (b) the disposal of the whole or substantially the whole of the university company's
-- undertaking or property; (c) the voluntary winding up of the university company; (d) the addition, deletion or alteration of any
-- provision of the constituent documents of the university company; and (e) the removal of any trustee from the Board."
-- (2): these apply "in addition to" the Companies Act 1967 and the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 requirements.
-- (3): "Any act done or agreement made in contravention of subsection (1) has no effect and is unenforceable at law."
DECLARE CompanyAct IS ONE OF
    `admitting a member of the company`
    `removing a member of the company`
    `selling substantially the whole undertaking`
    `selling one building`
    `winding up voluntarily`
    `amending the articles of association`
    `removing a trustee`
    `appointing a trustee`
    `hiring a lecturer`
    `signing a supply contract`

GIVEN `the act` IS A CompanyAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `needs the Minister's prior written consent` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `admitting a member of the company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removing a member of the company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling substantially the whole undertaking` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `winding up voluntarily` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `amending the articles of association` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removing a trustee` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 7(3), read with (1). Whether the act also satisfies the Companies Act or IRDA (s 7(2)) is outside this rule.
GIVEN `the act` IS A CompanyAct, `prior written consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act has effect under section 7` IF
    (NOT `needs the Minister's prior written consent` `the act`) OR `prior written consent was given`

§§ `8 -- what the State's money may be spent on`

-- s 8(2): "All moneys paid to the university company under subsection (1) may only be applied or expended by the university company
-- for such objects provided by its constituent documents as the Minister may allow."
GIVEN `the object is in the constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister allows the object` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `parliamentary moneys may be spent on the object` IF
    `the object is in the constituent documents` AND `the Minister allows the object`

§§ `9 -- information for the Minister, and the offence`

-- s 9(2): "The Minister or an authorised person may require ANY person to provide any information in that person's possession, or to
-- which that person has access" that is considered necessary for ascertaining whether the s 8 moneys were properly applied, or "any
-- other matters". (4): "Any person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with any requirement ... under subsection (2), or
-- who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays the Minister or an authorised person ... shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable
-- on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000." No imprisonment is provided. The text does not say who bears the burden on the excuse.
GIVEN `was required to give information` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave it` IS A BOOLEAN, `hindered or obstructed or delayed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits an offence under section 9` IF
        ((`was required to give information` AND (NOT `gave it`)) OR `hindered or obstructed or delayed`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

`maximum fine under section 9` MEANS 1000

`imprisonment is available under section 9` MEANS FALSE

§§ `10, 11 and 18 -- the Students' Union, and the Act over the company's own rules`

-- s 10(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act have effect in relation to any
-- student body constituted pursuant to the provisions of the constituent documents of the university company." (2): the Minister for
-- societies may by Gazette order exempt such a body from all or any of the provisions.
-- s 18: "On 1 April 2006, the students' association known as the Nanyang Technological University Students' Union and its
-- constituent bodies are deemed to be constituted pursuant to the provisions of the constituent documents of the university company."
DECLARE StudentBody IS ONE OF
    `the Students' Union`
    `a constituent body of the Students' Union`
    `a club set up under the constituent documents`
    `an informal study group`

GIVEN `the body` IS A StudentBody
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is constituted under the constituent documents` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `an informal study group` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- An order under s 10(2) may exempt from only some provisions; this rule answers whether the Societies Act applies at all, so a
-- partial exemption is treated as not exempt.
GIVEN `the body` IS A StudentBody, `wholly exempted by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Societies Act applies to the body` IF
    `is constituted under the constituent documents` `the body` AND (NOT `wholly exempted by Gazette order`)

-- s 11(1): a provision of the constituent documents, or a regulation made under them, "that is inconsistent with any provision of this
-- Act is, to the extent of the inconsistency, void."
GIVEN `inconsistent with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company rule is valid` IF NOT `inconsistent with the Act`

§§ `12(6), 12(7) and 15 -- litigation and contracts carried over`

-- s 12(6): "All proceedings by or against the predecessor university which were commenced before 1 April 2006 and which are pending
-- on that date may be continued, completed and enforced by or against the university company on and after that date."
GIVEN `commenced on` IS A NUMBER, `pending on the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceedings continue against the company` IF
    `commenced on` < `the appointed day` AND `pending on the appointed day`

-- s 15: all "deeds, contracts, schemes, bonds, agreements, instruments and arrangements subsisting immediately before 1 April 2006 to
-- which the predecessor university is a party continue in force ... and are enforceable by or against the university company as if
-- [it] had been named in them". s 12(7) says the same of agreements on transferred properties "whether or not of a nature that the
-- rights and liabilities under the agreement can be assigned". s 15 has no assignability qualifier and none is needed for it.
GIVEN `the predecessor university was a party` IS A BOOLEAN, `subsisting immediately before the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the contract forbids assignment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is enforceable by or against the company` IF
    `the predecessor university was a party` AND `subsisting immediately before the appointed day`

§§ `13 and 14 -- staff transferred`

-- s 13(1): "all persons employed immediately before that date by the predecessor university must be transferred to the service of the
-- university company on terms no less favourable than those enjoyed by them immediately prior to their transfer." (2): the old scheme
-- and terms continue to apply until the company draws up its own.
GIVEN `employed by the predecessor immediately before the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is transferred to the company` IF `employed by the predecessor immediately before the appointed day`

-- Reading monthly pay as one of the "terms" is an inference; the Act does not list terms.
GIVEN `pay before transfer` IS A NUMBER, `pay on transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer terms are no less favourable` IF `pay on transfer` >= `pay before transfer`

-- s 14(2): the company "must ... provide for the recognition of service under the predecessor university by that person to be service
-- under the university company." s 14(1), by contrast, only requires the company to "consider" earlier terms, "including any accrued
-- rights to leave".
GIVEN `transferred` IS A BOOLEAN, `years with the predecessor` IS A NUMBER, `years with the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recognised length of service` IS
    IF `transferred` THEN `years with the predecessor` + `years with the company`
                     ELSE `years with the company`

GIVEN `transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `accrued leave must be carried over in full` IF FALSE

GIVEN `transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `accrued leave must be considered` IF `transferred`

§§ `16 and 17 -- discipline carried over`

-- s 16(1): disciplinary proceedings "commenced before 1 April 2006 against -- (a) any employee of the predecessor university transferred
-- to the service of the university company under section 13; or (b) any student of the predecessor university, are pending on that
-- date, the proceedings must, on and after that date, be carried on and completed by the university company." (2), (3): a committee
-- hearing begun but undecided must be completed and its order is treated as the company's.
DECLARE Respondent IS ONE OF
    `a transferred employee`
    `a student of the predecessor university`
    `a contractor of the predecessor university`

GIVEN `the respondent` IS A Respondent, `commenced on` IS A NUMBER, `pending on the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company must complete the disciplinary proceedings` IF
        `commenced on` < `the appointed day`
    AND `pending on the appointed day`
    AND CONSIDER `the respondent`
        WHEN `a contractor of the predecessor university` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 17: the company "may reprimand, reduce in rank, retire, dismiss or punish in any other manner" a person who, while employed by the
-- predecessor, was "guilty of any misconduct or neglect of duty which would have rendered the person liable" to that punishment had
-- the person stayed with the predecessor and had the Act not been enacted.
GIVEN `misconduct while employed by the predecessor` IS A BOOLEAN, `would have been punishable by the predecessor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company may punish pre-transfer misconduct` IF
    `misconduct while employed by the predecessor` AND `would have been punishable by the predecessor`

§§ `19 and the Schedule -- the Register of Graduates`

-- Schedule para 1: the company "must maintain a Register of Graduates" of (a) "all persons who on 7 August 1980 were members of the
-- Guild of Graduates of the former Nanyang University and of all persons on whom degrees of that university had been conferred by
-- virtue of section 18(2) of the National University of Singapore Act"; (b) "all persons who immediately before 1 April 2006 were
-- members of the Guild of Graduates of the predecessor university, of all graduates of the National University of Singapore who were
-- matriculated students of the Nanyang Technological Institute before 1 July 1991 and of all persons on whom degrees of the
-- predecessor university had been conferred"; and (c) "all graduates of the University". Para 2: Parts A, B and C hold (a), (b) and
-- (c). Para 3: anyone on the Register "may receive such documents or other papers of the University as determined by the Board".
-- Para 4: "University" is the one operated by the university company.
DECLARE Graduate IS ONE OF
    `a Nanyang University Guild member on 7 August 1980`
    `a holder of a Nanyang University degree conferred under NUS Act s 18(2)`
    `a predecessor Guild member immediately before 1 April 2006`
    `an NUS graduate who matriculated at NTI before 1 July 1991`
    `an NUS graduate who matriculated at NTI on or after 1 July 1991`
    `a graduate of the predecessor university`
    `a graduate of the university company's University`
    `an NUS graduate who never studied at NTI`

DECLARE RegisterPart IS ONE OF
    `Part A`
    `Part B`
    `Part C`
    `not on the Register`

GIVEN `the graduate` IS A Graduate
GIVETH A RegisterPart
DECIDE `register part` IS
    CONSIDER `the graduate`
    WHEN `a Nanyang University Guild member on 7 August 1980` THEN `Part A`
    WHEN `a holder of a Nanyang University degree conferred under NUS Act s 18(2)` THEN `Part A`
    WHEN `a predecessor Guild member immediately before 1 April 2006` THEN `Part B`
    WHEN `an NUS graduate who matriculated at NTI before 1 July 1991` THEN `Part B`
    WHEN `a graduate of the predecessor university` THEN `Part B`
    WHEN `a graduate of the university company's University` THEN `Part C`
    OTHERWISE `not on the Register`

-- The 1 July 1991 cut-off as a date test, for an NUS graduate who matriculated at the Nanyang Technological Institute.
GIVEN `matriculated at NTI on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the NTI matriculant is on Part B` IF `matriculated at NTI on` < 19910701

GIVEN `the graduate` IS A Graduate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may receive University papers` IF
    NOT (`register part` `the graduate` EQUALS `not on the Register`)
